  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA (descriptive, verb-disciplined) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>Pakistan Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif announced June 12–14 that the United States and Iran finalized MOU text; a formal signing ceremony was scheduled for June 19 in Geneva; Iran President Pezeshkian confirmed the date to IRNA; Araghchi described a 14-point framework, with the first point being the lifting of the US naval blockade; Qatar and Pakistan served as co-mediators across five converging TIER1 outlets confirming the June 19 date (CNBC, CBS, NBC, Al Jazeera, Washington Post). → moved <span class="cite">F2</span>, <span class="cite">F8</span></p>

      <p>The last confirmed reciprocal strike cycle between Israel and Iran occurred June 7–8 — before F3's window opened June 10; no TIER1-confirmed direct IRGC strike on Israeli-claimed targets was documented in the June 10–17 period; US diplomatic intervention June 14–15 held Iranian retaliation in abeyance ahead of the June 19 ceremony. → moved <span class="cite">F3</span></p>

      <p>Commercial shipping through the Strait of Hormuz remained at approximately 5–10 transits per day against a pre-war baseline of approximately 94 per day per PortWatch and AIS data through mid-June; the MOU's Hormuz clause places a normalization framework at approximately July 19 — outside F4's July 2 horizon — while MCM timelines project weeks to months and war-risk P&amp;I cover remains suspended. → moved <span class="cite">F4</span></p>

      <p>Israeli forces struck Beirut's southern suburbs June 14; Iran's Khatam al-Anbiya Central Headquarters issued an explicit June 16 warning that continued Lebanese-front operations would draw a direct Iranian response, citing an MOU clause Iran interprets as requiring a halt to Israeli Lebanon operations — a reading both Jerusalem and Washington publicly dispute. → supports <span class="cite">F3</span>, <span class="cite">F8</span></p>

      <p>CENTCOM and TIER1 naval outlets confirmed MCM operations in the Strait of Hormuz commenced April 2026 with USS Pioneer (MCM-9) and USS Chief (MCM-14); commencement predated F5's window opening by approximately seven weeks, rendering the start-point criterion untestable — F5 retired as OBE per Judge ruling. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

      <p>Haredi Knesset parties (UTJ, Shas) remained in active parliamentary boycott over the Daycare Law as of June 17; a senior coalition figure told Times of Israel the law lacks majority support and will not advance; the dissolution bill's second and third readings remain unscheduled, and no election date has been inserted into the bill text. → moved <span class="cite">F6</span>, <span class="cite">F7</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

